Significance: patch
Type: fix
Comment: Developer advisory: get_starting_sales() no longer returns sales that have already ended. Because the starting loop no longer moves `_price` to the sale price, a completed sale already back at its regular price falls out of get_ending_sales() too, so on a store whose only matches were completed sales all four of wc_before/after_products_starting_sales and wc_before/after_products_ending_sales stop firing rather than firing with a shorter list. The daily `delete_transient( 'wc_products_onsale' )` and `WC_Cache_Helper::get_transient_version( 'product' )` bump sit inside the same guards and stop with them; both still run whenever a sale genuinely starts or ends. A listener treating the daily call as a heartbeat is no longer called.

Stop the daily scheduled-sales cron reprocessing every completed scheduled sale as both a starting and an ending sale.
